{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And all the people saw the voices.</b> I have already explained the sense of 'saw the voices': all sensations converge to one place. The meaning is that when they saw the voices and the torches — for it is the way of man to be frightened by them — and the sound of the shofar, such as was never heard in the world, and the mountain smoking alone, when they saw these wonders they trembled, like 'wandered and strayed' (Genesis 4:12), for each one departed from his station and drew backward; similarly 'the thresholds trembled' (Isaiah 6:4). The sense of אמות: the thresholds departed from their place whole; the prophet could not gauge them in the visions of prophecy. And one who says it means like זעו — this is not possible, for if they did not depart from their place, how did they stand afar off?"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {0 "Reading אמות as 'thresholds' (from אם/אמות = thresholds, as in Isaiah 6:4); the commentator who proposes זעו (= זעו, 'trembled') as an alternative reading is rejected. The syntax of the clause about the prophet is compressed and the subject ambiguous; rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:36:22.612459356Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}